  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REDD+ Investment Program Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The agreement is between Government of Ethiopia and the Royal Norwegian government. The current agreement is the continuation of the REDD+ investment phase I of the result based payment for Ethiopia to achieve  result based payment. Main objectives are to contribute to climate mitigation, climate adaptation and biodiversity conservation. Ethiopia has moved from REDD+ phase I to phase II of the bilateral Forest and Climate Partnership Agreement. Through RIP II Ethiopia is making investments on the ground with main target audience being local forest dwellers and communities, to eventually achieve phase III of the Partnership: verified carbon emission reductions from forest. Conserving and restoring forest in Ethiopia is contributing to increased resilience against the adverse effects of climate change, rural livelihoods and poverty reduction, maintained/increased water resources and to biodiversity. 

RIP phase II has an overarching goal to contribute to enhanced forest conservation by avoided deforestation and forest degradation, and to increased forest cover through tree planting and restoration of degraded forest areas. Particularly through the target related to increased forest cover, the program will also target national climate adaptation goals. The program also focuses beyond climate-related objectives, such as on provision of livelihoods, and social and environmental benefits for women, girls, youth, and other forest-dependent people, with the aim of protecting their rights, including equity and fair distribution of benefits. RIP II is contributing to forest conservation, landscape restoration and private sector engagement. It will also contribute to various SDGs such as climate actions and improved life on land.</narrative>
  </description>
